[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Every piece of software has predetermined what we could do with it. But what if software could generate itself as you interact with it? Introducing [music] Solaris, the first'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'interface world model. Solaris is [music] built to understand interaction and to run in real time. It generates [music] the interface itself frame by frame as you use it. No code'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'underneath, no layout to translate. The image is the application. [music] It treats your clicks and drags the way our video models treat words. Not as commands to look up, but as a signal for'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'what to generate next. Nothing about it is decided in advance. So nothing about it [music] has to stay the same. Light shifts, objects respond, the scene [music] answers to your intentions. It'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'becomes whatever you ask of it. And no two interactions are ever the same. Solaris isn\'t just changing how [music] humans experience interfaces. It\'s unlocking new ways for agents to'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'learn them, too. The need for fixed, hard-coded, and pre-rendered operating systems and surfaces are [music] soon to be a thing of the past. Solaris interfaces that are generated, not'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'coded.'
